  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "New benchmarks show simple baselines, label quality and stage-wise filtration often matter more than model novelty across molecular ML tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is controlled evaluation of molecular ML, with attention shifting from architecture to benchmark design and label quality. PeptSol provides 1388 curated protected-peptide solubility measurements with chemistry-aware splits for seven frozen encoders. Ark-ADMET finds that representation and hyperparameter choice are endpoint-specific under the TDC protocol, matching or beating leaderboard scores on 7 of 21 endpoints. The immunogenicity study reports that a format lookup beats sequence predictors on ADA% labels. The DiffDock study finds no gain from focused or mixed torsional supervision, and HEDGEHOG reveals stage-wise attrition among 22 generators on KRAS G12D that standard metrics miss. The antibody-agent paper similarly compares agents against a Bayesian optimization baseline. Not every item is a benchmark; several are method papers.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
